  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This small-leaved cultivar forms a semidwarf bushshaped plant, maturing at 2.5-3 m tall. The leaves are a pale yellow green with a rather thin texture and a slight hint of rusty red on the extreme edges. They measure about 4 cm long and 4-5 cm across. Each leaf is divided three-quarters of the way to the leaf base into five lanceolate lobes which terminate in long, slender, sharp tips. The two basal lobes often have tiny spur lobes. The lobe edges bend slightly upwards, and the margins are irregularly toothed. The name 'Saotome' means \"rice-planting girl.\""
  },
